{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3653","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3653","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3653\",\"parent_revision\":\"4c0dc50e1ab8ef816136acffd1b713a7ca52ac37e78ea05cb9a02a07aab03532\",\"root_revision\":\"4c0dc50e1ab8ef816136acffd1b713a7ca52ac37e78ea05cb9a02a07aab03532\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nGroom swarm agents write file:line citations and quotations to backlog items that do not match the source they cite. The item keeps the wrong citation as fact until someone checks it by hand.\\n\\nObserved in one groom of #3060 (all against origin/main a75f11f0a):\\n- fact-checker cited `backlog_core/server.py:2306-2309` for `_hint` (actual 2101-2104), `server.py:2352-2392` for `_build_over_budget_view` (actual def at 2147), and `docs/component-architecture.md:1278-1286` for a quote that is in `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:1278-1286`.\\n- classifier cited `disclosure_handler.py:487-490` as the `next_call` hint (it is NavigateResponse construction; `next_call` is at 549-563) and \\\"callsite 2143\\\" (a line inside `_sections_index_from_result`, not a callsite).\\n- rtica-assessor carried 2026-08-20 line numbers (`server.py:2306-2309`, `2379-2387`) into a 2026-09-19 condition.\\n- alignment-analyst misquoted the repo owner's five open items as four different items.\\n- impact-analyst stated that PR #3649's narrowed `_usage` \\\"avoids naming navigate=/map=-derived fields\\\"; the code at dc5b6d264:server.py:2174-2182 names navigate=, head= and skip_tokens=.\\n\\nEach error was found only because the orchestrator checked the cited line by hand. The next stage (RT-ICA, groomer, planner) reads these sections as verified input.\\n\\nImpact: planning and implementation agents act on wrong locations and wrong quotes; one wrong statement (the impact-analyst one) had already been copied into a delegation prompt before it was caught.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: the agents copy line numbers from earlier item entries or recall instead of reading the cited line in the current revision, and nothing checks a citation before the write.\\n\\nExpected: every file:line and quotation an agent writes to a backlog item resolves to the quoted text at the stated revision.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation, re-groom of #3060, 2026-09-19\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d85d2bf11bb32975b70f79a9dbe5bf05d85b61ae6dfdd1b10c4cf0741370d7e3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVoHyLg\"}"}